### Highlights by District

**D3/D5 — Queenstown (Rank 1)**
The stealth performer. 30,000 one-north STEM jobs are the engine; Queenstown 5-room HDB is hitting $4,500/month. Near-zero new rental supply — mature estate, no BTO in pipeline. Landlords on 2022 contracts are significantly underpriced at renewal.

**D15 — East Coast / Katong (Rank 2)**
TEL Stage 4 is the catalyst — first rail access in a previously MRT-dark corridor repriced everything. Expat family demand spiked post-TEL; sales prices adjusted faster than rental contracts. Clients renewing here should push 10–15% above prior contract.

**D20 — Bishan / Toa Payoh (Rank 3)**
Low-volatility, high-durability rental income. School cluster (Ai Tong, CHIJ St. Nicholas, Tao Nan) locks in family tenants who won't move. The HDB upgrader wait-out period also concentrates interim rental demand here.

**D14/13 — Paya Lebar / Geylang (Rank 4)**
Geylang HDB 5-room clocked +7.9% in 3Q2025 — highest single-estate datapoint in ERA's dataset. Triple MRT interchange, Paya Lebar Quarter jobs, and the airbase relocation narrative converging. Contrarian pitch for investor-cohort clients before the rezoning story breaks formally.

**D22 — Jurong East / Lakeside (Rank 5)**
A 2027–2029 thesis, not a 2026 cashflow play. JLD second-CBD designation + JRL construction are structural catalysts, but timeline risk is real. Route D22 enquiries through a cashflow stress-test before recommending to yield-dependent clients.

---

### Action Flags for Your Book

1. **Lease renewal pricing** — D5, D15, D20 landlords on 2022–2023 contracts are 12–18% below current market. Any lease expiring in 6 months needs benchmarking now.
2. **D14/13 investor note** — below-RCR pricing with above-RCR momentum and an airbase rezoning catalyst. Strong candidate for a dedicated client note to the investor cohort.
3. **D22 caveat** — always pair with a cashflow stress-test; it's a hold play, not a yield play.


